# Prettier scope for My MaNaGeR.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (Wave 8.7, 2026-10-07).
# `npm run verify:prettier` runs `prettier --check .`, and Prettier honours
# this file automatically. Without it the check either swept build artifacts
# and dependencies or, worse, silently matched nothing and reported success -
# a gate that never fails proves nothing.

# ---- build artifacts, dependencies, scratch -----------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
.wrangler/
tmp/
_archive/
vendor/

# ---- HTML is deliberately NOT Prettier-managed --------------------------
# Reformatting a served page rewrites its inline <script> blocks, which
# invalidates the SHA-256 CSP hashes held in worker.js and serve.cjs
# (AGENTS.md rule 1 - stale hashes block the page with no visible error).
# HTML markup is owned by the a11y gate (tools/verify-a11y-labels.cjs) and
# the per-page browser harnesses.
*.html

# ---- hash-pinned skill bundles ------------------------------------------
# skills-lock.json pins each skill's content hash and tools/verify-skills-lock.cjs
# fails on a mismatch, so reformatting a skill would break the lock.
.agents/

# ---- data, config and generated reports ---------------------------------
# JSON/JSONC are not code-style managed here: wrangler*.jsonc carries comments
# that Prettier's JSON parser would drop, and the gate-matrix/calc-golden files
# are generated or captured data rather than source.
**/*.json
**/*.jsonc
mcp/fixtures/

# js/jic-rates-full.js is GENERATED from JIC_Rate_Book_2025-2027_FULL.md by
# tools/gen-jic-full.cjs (same class as projects-data.js / demo-data.js below:
# data, not hand-written source). Nobody edits it by hand - the header says so
# and `npm run verify:jic` fails if it drifts from the generator. Prettier
# would expand the one-row-per-line rate array to one OBJECT per line, taking
# the file from 101 KB to 166 KB (15.9 KB to 17.9 KB gzipped) for no change in
# behaviour, and the owner asked for the calculator to stay quick on a slow
# connection - so it stays compact and out of the style gate.
js/jic-rates-full.js

# ---- CI-generated artifacts (not source) --------------------------------
# The gitleaks step runs BEFORE this gate and writes its SARIF report into the
# workspace. Prettier infers the JSON parser for `.sarif`, so an unformatted
# generated report failed the gate on Actions while passing locally, where the
# file never exists. Found 2026-10-07 on the first CI run of this gate.
*.sarif
gitleaks-*

# ---- docs and non-code assets -------------------------------------------
*.md
**/*.md
